## Prerequisites

### 1. Toolchain

- `agent-browser` CLI installed — verify with `agent-browser --version`.
- `bash` 4 or newer — verify with `bash --version`.
- `jq` (only if you parse the subagent JSON yourself) — verify with `jq --version`.

Reload the live agent-browser workflow at the start of every session
(commands evolve across versions; never invoke from memory):

```bash
agent-browser skills get core
# Electron desktop targets only:
agent-browser skills get electron
```

### 2. Required system state (the script will NOT start these)

- **Chrome / Chromium running with remote-debugging enabled.** The
  script attaches via `--auto-connect` and refuses to spawn a fresh
  browser. Recommended dedicated profile:

  ```bash
  google-chrome \
    --user-data-dir="$HOME/.chrome-e2e" \
    --remote-debugging-port=9222
  ```

- **The target application running** (e.g. `npm run dev`,
  `electron .`, `docker compose up`). The script will NOT start it
  (avoids polluting the user's shell — see `harness-kit:e2e/SKILL.md`
  § Connection Failure Protocol).

If either is missing the script fails fast with a connection error,
which is **not** a valid OUTER RED.

### 3. Environment variables

| Variable               | Purpose                                                                                          | Required when                          | Default                              |
|------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------|--------------------------------------|
| `E2E_TS_OVERRIDE`      | Pin the run timestamp (so a Phase 2 destructive re-dispatch regenerates the same `ack_token`).   | Phase 2 of any destructive AS          | `$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ)`         |
| `E2E_DESTRUCTIVE_ACK`  | Phase 2 ack token (`<AS>-<slug>-<ts>`) provided by the user as `proceed-destructive <token>`.    | Phase 2 of any destructive AS          | unset                                |

You should rarely set these by hand — the `harness-kit:e2e` subagent
dispatch flow injects them. Set them yourself ONLY when reproducing
a Phase 2 run from the shell to debug.

If this feature adds extra env vars (test tenant id, sandbox API
key, etc.), append them as new rows; one row per variable; no `...`.

## Running

### Run a single AS-N

```bash
./tests/e2e/<feature>.sh AS-1
```

This is the only supported form. There is no "run everything" mode
at the script level — orchestration is the caller's job.

| Exit code | Meaning                                                              | Next step                                                  |
|-----------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------|
| `0`       | Scenario passed.                                                     | Done. Evidence still written for audit.                    |
| `64`      | Unknown `AS-N` (typo, or scenario not yet implemented in the script).| Fix the arg or add the `case AS-N)` branch.                |
| `75`      | Hit a destructive gate; awaiting Phase 2 ack.                        | See **Destructive scenarios** below.                       |
| other     | Real RED, or environment broken.                                     | If env: see Troubleshooting. If RED: drive the inner loop. |

Evidence (screenshots at every assertion boundary, a11y snapshot on
failure, video if configured, plain-text `result.txt`) is written to:

```
tests/e2e/.evidence/<feature>/<UTC-timestamp>-AS-N/
```

That path is `.gitignore`d on first scaffold (see
`harness-kit:e2e/SKILL.md` § First-Run Setup). Never commit it.
Disk cleanup is the user's call only — no skill in harness-kit
deletes evidence on the user's behalf.

### Destructive scenarios (two-phase flow)

When `AS-N` reaches a `_destructive_gate` line, Phase 1 prints:

```
DESTRUCTIVE_GATE: action=<desc>; url=<url>; resource=<resource>; ack_token=<token>
```

…and exits `75`. The user replies (literal):

```
proceed-destructive <token>
```

The subagent re-dispatches Phase 2 with both env vars set:

```bash
E2E_TS_OVERRIDE=<original-utc-timestamp> \
E2E_DESTRUCTIVE_ACK=<token> \
./tests/e2e/<feature>.sh AS-N
```

Each gate gets its own token — agreeing to delete an account does
not transitively authorize five steps of follow-up destruction.
Full protocol: `harness-kit:e2e/reference/destructive-gate-protocol.md`.

### How NOT to run

- ✗ `./tests/e2e/<feature>.sh` (no AS arg) — exits with usage error.
- ✗ Drop `--auto-connect` / `${AB_FLAGS}` from any `agent-browser`
  call — the subagent rejects reports with `auto_connect_used: false`.
- ✗ `rm -rf tests/e2e/.evidence/...` between runs — destroys the
  debugging trail and is the user's decision only.
- ✗ Run inline in the parent agent context — must be dispatched via
  the `e2e-subagent` marker (see SKILL.md § Subagent Execution).
- ✗ Hand-edit the script during the inner-TDD loop — the script is
  the OUTER RED specification; only Step 5 (Verify OUTER GREEN)
  re-runs it.

## Troubleshooting

| Symptom                                              | Cause                                                          | Fix                                                                                                  |
|------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `could not attach to Chrome`                         | Chrome not running, or no `--remote-debugging-port`.           | Re-launch Chrome per Prerequisites § 2.                                                              |
| Connection error to target URL / Electron process    | Target app not running.                                        | Start the app yourself, then retry. The skill will NOT start it for you.                             |
| Test fails at "element `<x>` not found"              | Real RED (good!) or genuine a11y regression in the UI.         | Missing feature → drive the inner TDD loop. Genuine a11y bug → fix the UI labels, not the test.      |
| `unknown scenario: AS-X`                             | Typo, or `case AS-X)` branch not yet implemented.              | Check the `case` block in `tests/e2e/<feature>.sh`.                                                  |
| Phase 2 ack token mismatch                           | `E2E_TS_OVERRIDE` not pinned to Phase 1's timestamp.           | Re-dispatch with the original UTC ts — see Destructive scenarios above.                              |
| Evidence dir not created                             | `mkdir -p` failed, or test exited before the setup line.       | Check disk perms; re-run; if persists, suspect the script was edited.                                |

